      "pronunciationText": "Yes, it's still chlorine, because it still has seventeen protons. The difference is in the neutrons. Thirty-seven minus seventeen gives twenty, two more than chlorine-thirty-five's eighteen. Atoms of the same element with different numbers of neutrons are called isotopes. And because both have seventeen electrons, arranged the same way, they react in essentially the same way. Chemistry is mostly about electrons, and neutrons hardly change it.",
